                <pb facs="0214" n="124" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg124"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1608</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vladivostok</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vladivostok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-17T19:00:00+08:47"><hi rendition="#italic">April 17, 1918,
                                7 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 17, 2.56 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Chinese cruiser arrived to-day to protect Chinese residents. Will remain
                    indefinitely.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
